import VersoManual

open Verso.Genre Manual

#doc (Manual) "About the Course" =>

%%%
tag := "about"
%%%

Verified systems programming connects executable implementations with precise specifications
and machine-checked proofs. In this course, we will explore that connection with the help of
proof agents.

These notes will document the ideas, techniques, and reasoning behind the course's main artifact.
They will grow alongside the course.

# Course Repositories

%%%
tag := "repositories"
%%%

The [course website repository](https://github.com/plum-umd/cmsc818c) contains the Verso sources
for these pages and the workflow that publishes them.

The main course artifact will be developed in a separate repository, with its own build and
verification workflow. The notes can link to particular revisions there as the material evolves.
